                <pb facs="0750" n="618" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg618"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7541: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-07-30T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30, 1926—7
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 31—12:56
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>311. Legation’s 304, July 26, noon. Following telegram has been received from the
                    American consul general at Canton: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“July 29, 2 p.m. Referring to telegram of July 23, noon. Cantonese
                            authorities now predict capture of Hankow and Wuchang in 10 days.
                            General Chiang of Whampoa Cadets has left Canton for the Hunan
                            front.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
